DESCRIPTION<<VER_4_1_0_P0_P2
4.1.0: P0–P2 module integration — wire contract bundles into hosted core paths.

Memory (kernel/core/memory/): fl_stack free-frame pool for PMM; fl_exec_context with
heap/stack/instruction-pointer/register snapshot; fl_result_t on fallible PMM APIs.

Time (kernel/core/time/): fl_timekeeping uses POSIX time.h (CLOCK_MONOTONIC) per P1-7.

Identity (kernel/core/identity/): SQLite accounts (userland/shell/fl_users.db) with
SHA-256 salted password hashes (userland/identity/password_hash.cpp). Defaults:
flinstone/flinstone (normal) and root/root (elevated). login switches account.

Jail (P0 FS surface): only elevated login or `sudo <command>` escapes VM jail
(e.g. sudo cd /path); plain `sudo` grants a token for protected paths only.

Authz (P2-3): fm_service gates; non-elevated users enter their password for sudo/sudo -i;
su/su -/su -c switch or run commands with the target account password; useradd/userdel/passwd.
logout returns to the default user; sudo -k revokes elevation tokens without changing account.

Password hashes use OpenSSL PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 (record stores iteration count); legacy
stretch/single SHA-256 rows still verify. login/su/sudo read passwords on the next line.
AArch64 CI cross-build: ./deps/fetch-openssl-aarch64.sh supplies libcrypto headers/libs
(deps/install-aarch64) alongside fetch-sqlite-aarch64.sh.
P2-3/P2-4: guest denies three privileged subsystem ops; shell cmd→subsystem op mapping;
elevation grant/revoke audit lines (who/when/reason) when FL_AUDIT is set.
Tests: test_p0_p2_wiring (stack, PMM, exec context, user db, path props, timekeeping, authz).
VER_4_1_0_P0_P2

RELEASE_DATE=2026-05-21
